WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:03.650
Wealth, fame, power...

3
00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:04.440
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

4
00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:07.820
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates, obtained everything the world has to offer.

5
00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:07.360
attained this and everything else
the world had to offer.

6
00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:10.820
And his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

7
00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:11.660
What he said in his final moments drove countless souls to the seas.

8
00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:13.660
You want my treasure?

9
00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:13.700
You can have it!

10
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:15.450
Go ahead.

11
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:17.040
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

12
00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:16.660
Find it!

13
00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.250
Everything is right where I left it!

14
00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.250
Now you just have to find it!

15
00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.750
These words lured
men to the Grand Line

16
00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:26.380
People set their sights on the Grand Line in pursuit of their dreams.

17
00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:26.920
in pursuit of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine!

18
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:29.630
The world has truly entered the Great Pirate Era!

19
00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.850
This is the time known as
the Great Pirate Era!

20
00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:35.640
Come aboard and bring along all your hopes and dreams

21
00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:41.440
I know together we'll find everything we're looking for

22
00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:42.690
One Piece!

23
00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:52.700
Compasses? Not for me. Left them all behind

24
00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:58.500
I'm headed out to sea, with my heart serving as guide

25
00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:04.540
Following the ancient map to the spot marked "X" reveals

26
00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:09.760
Yeah, it's only legendary till someone proves it's real

27
00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:13.710
When the world's got you down,

28
00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:16.850
lean on your crew, they'll turn it around

29
00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:22.190
Their biorhythm will carry you through

30
00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.230
We're gonna make the most of it

31
00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:31.400
Come aboard and bring along all your hopes and dreams

32
00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:36.990
I know together we'll find everything we're looking for

33
00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:40.040
Got some change to my name,

34
00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:43.250
and maybe you wanna be my friend?

35
00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:48.130
We are, we are on the cruise!

36
00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:49.760
WE ARE!

37
00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:58.390
<b>Arlong Park</b>

38
00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:22.120
This weather's perfect!

39
00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:27.210
So which way is the Grand Line?

40
00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:29.250
Is it that way?

41
00:02:30.070 --> 00:02:33.040
Or maybe... this way?

42
00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:35.390
That way. Over here.
Maybe there? I dunno.

43
00:02:35.390 --> 00:02:38.350
Where could it be? I wanna
see this place! I wanna see!

44
00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:39.680
You need to sit.

45
00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:41.140
Geez... you bug me.

46
00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:46.810
Oh, sorry. Heh! I'm just excited
that we finally got a cook on board.

47
00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:48.900
Now we just need Nami.

48
00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:51.730
Then nothing will stand between
us and the Grand Line!

49
00:02:51.970 --> 00:02:58.030
Nami, ah... I could just sit around all day
and think about how beautiful she is...

50
00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:00.330
I can't wait till I
get to see her again.

51
00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:05.370
So. Are we getting close
to where Nami is?

52
00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:07.570
You know, the island?

53
00:03:07.570 --> 00:03:10.440
You're way too naïve and way too young!

54
00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:11.610
Don't you get it?!

55
00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:16.840
Don't you realize every second that passes
brings us closer to the infamous Arlong?!

56
00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:22.170
Nami couldn't stop
looking at Arlong's picture

57
00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:24.850
when she saw it. And it
wasn't a normal kinda stare.

58
00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:28.810
There was something different
about the way she was staring.

59
00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:30.360
Something focused.

60
00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:36.990
I'm telling you, Nami's
planning on taking down Arlong

61
00:03:36.990 --> 00:03:39.370
and then collecting the
twenty million-berry bounty.

62
00:03:39.390 --> 00:03:41.370
For all we know,
while we just sit here,

63
00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:43.950
she's already making her
way through his compound!

64
00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:46.960
That's nice. Let's eat.

65
00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:47.750
Sounds good.

66
00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:51.160
Don't tell me you guys are so clueless

67
00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:53.870
that you have actually never
heard of the evil Arlong?

68
00:03:53.870 --> 00:03:55.910
Uh, no. So who is he?

69
00:03:55.910 --> 00:03:56.760
Yeah.

70
00:04:01.360 --> 00:04:06.680
Listen up, boys! Time for your education
on the cunning shark that is Arlong!

71
00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:09.940
Arlong is a fishman who used to
destroy everything in his path

72
00:04:10.060 --> 00:04:11.190
up and down the Grand Line.

73
00:04:11.330 --> 00:04:11.860
Fishman?

74
00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:14.820
That's cool. I don't think I've
ever met one of those before.

75
00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:18.360
I've heard that the females on
Fishman Island are some of the most

76
00:04:18.770 --> 00:04:21.040
beautiful creatures in
the world to behold.

77
00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:22.410
Fishman sounds weird...

78
00:04:22.900 --> 00:04:24.120
Do they look like this?

79
00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:28.790
Can't you focus
for just one minute, please!

80
00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:32.410
Alright... I will start
from the very beginning.

81
00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:35.580
The reason they call the Grand Line
a pirate graveyard in the first place

82
00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:39.470
is because of Arlong and the other
two powers like him who rule over it.

83
00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:43.850
The first of the powers are known
as the Seven Warlords of the Sea!

84
00:04:46.610 --> 00:04:48.230
Seven Warlords?

85
00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:51.690
The Seven Warlords are pirates
authorized by the government.

86
00:04:51.900 --> 00:04:53.100
Seriously...?

87
00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:57.110
Why would any pirate on the sea
want government approval?

88
00:04:57.460 --> 00:04:58.740
For protection.

89
00:04:58.760 --> 00:05:02.230
The government looks the other way
in exchange for a cut of their treasure,

90
00:05:02.230 --> 00:05:04.120
and they're allowed to exist.

91
00:05:04.130 --> 00:05:06.710
'Course to other pirates
they're just government dogs.

92
00:05:06.710 --> 00:05:09.280
But they didn't get to where
they are by being weak.

93
00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:12.040
These guys are powerful.

94
00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:20.550
The man who defeated
Zoro is one of these Warlords.

95
00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:22.590
His name is Hawkeye Mihawk.

96
00:05:22.910 --> 00:05:24.390
That's so cool!

97
00:05:24.510 --> 00:05:26.780
I can't wait to meet all
seven of these guys!

98
00:05:26.780 --> 00:05:28.600
They sound awesome!

99
00:05:28.910 --> 00:05:32.600
Yeah... Well, the first among the Warlords,
at least first you should know about,

100
00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:34.560
is Jinbei, captain of the fishmen.

101
00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:38.110
He is dangerous like
no one you've ever known...

102
00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:42.570
Easily causing as much havoc and
destruction around the Grand Line as Arlong.

103
00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:45.830
Is this closer?

104
00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:48.790
That looks just like your last
picture only standing up.

105
00:05:48.980 --> 00:05:53.530
Arlong has taken control of over twenty
towns since coming to the East Blue.

106
00:05:53.530 --> 00:05:55.630
His strength easily
surpasses anyone you've

107
00:05:55.630 --> 00:05:57.750
encountered including
that of Don Krieg's...

108
00:05:57.770 --> 00:05:59.130
He's devastating.

109
00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:03.960
So why do you think Nami would go
after this guy, all by herself, huh?

110
00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:07.220
I told you already, she wants
to collect the bounty on his head.

111
00:06:07.550 --> 00:06:10.560
Oh, wouldn't it be great
if Nami was a mermaid?

112
00:06:10.580 --> 00:06:14.190
I'd give anything to see that!

113
00:06:14.440 --> 00:06:18.190
<b>Nami</b>

114
00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:15.940
She'd look like this.

115
00:06:15.940 --> 00:06:18.440
Tear that thing up... or die!

116
00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:21.940
Have either of you morons heard
a single word that I've said to you?!

117
00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:23.080
Sure. Badass fishmen.

118
00:06:23.080 --> 00:06:25.660
Some guy's stronger than some
other guy. We get it.

119
00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:27.830
No, you don't get it.

120
00:06:27.830 --> 00:06:30.380
You've never had to face a fishman.

121
00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:34.080
Well, uh... we will when we get
there so don't worry about it.

122
00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:37.500
I guess
I'll get lunch started.

123
00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:39.670
'Bout time! Let's eat!

124
00:06:39.760 --> 00:06:40.980
What? Food?

125
00:06:40.980 --> 00:06:42.710
What're you in the mood for?

126
00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:44.770
I want meat right off the bone!

127
00:06:44.770 --> 00:06:46.720
I want sautéed bean sprouts!

128
00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:48.680
Okay, leave it to me.

129
00:06:50.320 --> 00:06:51.430
This won't take long.

130
00:06:51.780 --> 00:06:53.600
Meat and bean sprouts, no prob.

131
00:06:53.610 --> 00:06:57.400
Man, having a cook is
the best! Huh? Huh?!

132
00:06:57.450 --> 00:06:58.650
It sure is.

133
00:06:58.650 --> 00:07:00.850
Bring me meat! Lots of meat!

134
00:07:00.850 --> 00:07:03.490
Sprouts! I want
bean sprouts! Bean sprouts!

135
00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:09.740
<b>Northwestern East Blue</b>

136
00:07:16.590 --> 00:07:20.290
Here's this month's
take. I hope you enjoy it.

137
00:07:20.340 --> 00:07:26.010
<b>Captain Nezumi
16th Branch, Marines</b>

138
00:07:20.930 --> 00:07:24.090
Ah, Arlong.
You are so much smarter

139
00:07:24.100 --> 00:07:26.880
than your regular
run-of-the-mill pirate.

140
00:07:27.170 --> 00:07:28.760
You know how the world works.

141
00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:33.390
<b>Captain "Sawtooth" Arlong
(Saw Shark Fishman)
Arlong Pirates</b>

142
00:07:31.850 --> 00:07:35.730
Likewise. There aren't many Marine
captains who know that befriending me means

143
00:07:35.740 --> 00:07:37.730
they can milk the
East Blue for eternity.

144
00:07:38.410 --> 00:07:42.920
The fact that you understand makes you more
like me, than any other Marine out here.

145
00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:44.320
Thank you very much.

146
00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:47.910
Don't thank me, thank money!

147
00:07:48.420 --> 00:07:50.660
It's the only thing you can
count on in this world.

148
00:07:51.410 --> 00:07:55.040
It's more reliable than people,
that's for sure.

149
00:07:55.130 --> 00:07:56.580
Don't you agree?

150
00:07:56.710 --> 00:07:58.710
Of course.

151
00:07:58.930 --> 00:08:00.920
As a rule I hate all humans,

152
00:08:01.050 --> 00:08:03.670
but you are the one tolerable
exception that I've found.

153
00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:06.970
Well... if you'll excuse me.

154
00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:09.930
Why not stay awhile and
have a drink with me?

155
00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:14.140
I would, but the longer a Marine
cruiser stays docked at a pirate island,

156
00:08:14.150 --> 00:08:15.890
the quicker we get unwanted attention.

157
00:08:16.220 --> 00:08:17.940
I'll kill anyone who reports you.

158
00:08:18.120 --> 00:08:19.690
Everybody knows that.

159
00:08:19.690 --> 00:08:22.000
Thank you,
but still, we must go.

160
00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:24.190
Hey, the captain is leaving!

161
00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:26.320
Escort him back to his ship.

162
00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:31.870
<b>Officer Hatchan
(Octopus Fishman)
Arlong Pirates</b>

163
00:08:26.970 --> 00:08:27.860
Yes, sir.

164
00:08:29.540 --> 00:08:31.870
The pot's back that way... Hop in.

165
00:08:32.010 --> 00:08:34.450
Thank you! That's very kind of you.

166
00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:37.830
When I see your face, it always
makes me want to laugh. It's funny.

167
00:08:38.170 --> 00:08:39.080
You look like a rat.

168
00:08:41.670 --> 00:08:43.960
Hey, Hatchan, watch your mouth now.

169
00:08:44.040 --> 00:08:45.800
The captain's our honored guest.

170
00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:48.300
Oh, right, sorry about that.

171
00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:50.340
Don't worry about it.

172
00:08:54.570 --> 00:08:55.970
Here we go, men.

173
00:08:56.540 --> 00:09:00.240
These fishmen are
disgusting. Such a vile group.

174
00:09:00.240 --> 00:09:02.440
But they sure do pay well.

175
00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:06.900
<b>East Gate, Arlong Park</b>

176
00:09:17.670 --> 00:09:19.540
Hey, you. Get outta my way!

177
00:09:19.940 --> 00:09:22.910
Arlong's going to die today!

178
00:09:22.910 --> 00:09:26.750
He killed my daddy and so now
I'm gonna have to kill him!

179
00:09:28.110 --> 00:09:31.050
So move, or I'll have to kill you too.

180
00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:32.430
Hey!

181
00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:37.350
Now...

182
00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:39.430
You should know that Arlong
doesn't have time to deal with

183
00:09:39.430 --> 00:09:41.640
whimpering little punks like you.

184
00:09:42.650 --> 00:09:44.610
You're too young. Go home.

185
00:09:46.510 --> 00:09:49.990
Take that with you and use it
to keep yourself out of trouble, kid.

186
00:09:50.990 --> 00:09:52.700
Go to hell.

187
00:09:59.800 --> 00:10:01.500
Nami! You've returned!

188
00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:04.220
I haven't seen you around
here for quite a while.

189
00:10:04.220 --> 00:10:06.270
So, how did you do this time?

190
00:10:06.270 --> 00:10:08.240
Heh. Who are you talking to?

191
00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:12.380
You know, I can't believe the world is
full of such blind idiots... Wanna see?

192
00:10:14.210 --> 00:10:17.010
You, girl, are one excellent liar.

193
00:10:17.050 --> 00:10:18.180
That's true.

194
00:10:18.720 --> 00:10:21.930
Listen up, everybody!
Nami's finally returned!

195
00:10:21.950 --> 00:10:23.140
Time for a party!

196
00:10:28.190 --> 00:10:31.070
<b>Officer Nami
Arlong Pirates</b>

197
00:10:47.720 --> 00:10:52.760
Alright. We're here.
That's Arlong Park ahead.

198
00:10:54.660 --> 00:10:57.130
Arlong Park, huh?
So this is the hideout of

199
00:10:57.130 --> 00:10:59.850
Arlong the Fishman Pirate
from the Grand Line?!

200
00:11:01.520 --> 00:11:04.270
I hope Nami's really here.

201
00:11:04.840 --> 00:11:07.510
Big Sis Nami's ship
was the Going Merry,

202
00:11:07.510 --> 00:11:10.270
so before we do anything stupid,
we should quietly check

203
00:11:10.270 --> 00:11:12.230
to see if it stopped
on this island first.

204
00:11:12.340 --> 00:11:13.530
Yeah. Good idea.

205
00:11:19.060 --> 00:11:20.450
Let's attack.

206
00:11:21.920 --> 00:11:25.220
But I just said we shouldn't
do anything stupid!

207
00:11:25.220 --> 00:11:26.870
What?! Attack?! You idiot!

208
00:11:27.060 --> 00:11:29.090
We know nothing about this place!

209
00:11:29.090 --> 00:11:31.250
Yeah, these guys are the fishmen!

210
00:11:31.420 --> 00:11:33.260
We need some kinda plan to do that!

211
00:11:33.390 --> 00:11:36.300
While the two of you are
busy blabbering and wimping out,

212
00:11:36.320 --> 00:11:39.260
I'm placing my thoughts on the
battle we're about to face.

213
00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:42.390
Luffy told me to bring her
back and I'll do just that.

214
00:11:44.020 --> 00:11:44.980
Let's go!

215
00:11:51.780 --> 00:11:53.570
There it is!

216
00:11:53.750 --> 00:11:56.900
Ha! Found it! The Going Merry.
It's right over there.

217
00:11:56.920 --> 00:11:58.790
Then she has to be on
the island somewhere.

218
00:11:58.790 --> 00:12:00.370
We just have to find her.

219
00:12:00.460 --> 00:12:02.950
What do you think you're doing?!
Would you idiots untie me!

220
00:12:02.960 --> 00:12:04.870
I am not the enemy!

221
00:12:05.360 --> 00:12:09.010
We're east of Arlong
Park, here at Cocoyashi Village.

222
00:12:09.010 --> 00:12:10.290
But it's strange.

223
00:12:10.610 --> 00:12:13.630
Why would she have stopped
so far from the village?

224
00:12:13.870 --> 00:12:15.840
Untie me, dammit!

225
00:12:15.910 --> 00:12:17.630
Zoro, you're hurt way too bad

226
00:12:17.650 --> 00:12:21.470
to be of any help when we go ashore.
Just sit tight and relax.

227
00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:26.100
It's okay. Rest up.
You can help next time.

228
00:12:28.400 --> 00:12:31.570
One of these days I'm gonna
skewer him like a piece of meat!

229
00:12:31.570 --> 00:12:34.690
Fear not, gentlemen. I will
bring the girl back safely!

230
00:12:36.370 --> 00:12:40.110
Looks like skipping Arlong
Park has sure cheered you up.

231
00:12:40.580 --> 00:12:41.820
Prepare the anchor!

232
00:12:41.820 --> 00:12:44.660
Bring us alongside the Going Merry!

233
00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:46.920
Aye!

234
00:12:46.920 --> 00:12:49.710
Yes!
Now that we're under way,

235
00:12:49.710 --> 00:12:51.850
it's time to give a name to this voyage.

236
00:12:51.850 --> 00:12:55.130
I think I shall call it, "The
Great Adventures of Captain Usopp."

237
00:13:04.860 --> 00:13:07.470
What is it? What'd you see?!

238
00:13:07.660 --> 00:13:09.980
It's fishmen!

239
00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:11.520
Full speed ahead.

240
00:13:11.830 --> 00:13:12.940
Okeydoke.

241
00:13:15.470 --> 00:13:17.140
Why didn't we just dock right there?!

242
00:13:17.140 --> 00:13:18.840
Shh!

243
00:13:18.840 --> 00:13:19.950
Didn't you see that?

244
00:13:19.970 --> 00:13:22.870
There were three fishmen
over there. It's Arlong's crew.

245
00:13:22.880 --> 00:13:25.080
We can't stop here right now.

246
00:13:25.180 --> 00:13:26.980
Do not yell at me!

247
00:13:26.980 --> 00:13:31.140
If there are fishmen here, this entire
area must be under Arlong's control.

248
00:13:31.140 --> 00:13:32.670
So what now?

249
00:13:32.710 --> 00:13:36.020
Huh. We could just
say we couldn't find her.

250
00:13:36.020 --> 00:13:39.920
Untie me now, morons! Come on!

251
00:13:40.460 --> 00:13:42.500
Huh.
Never seen that boat before.

252
00:13:42.500 --> 00:13:43.340
Suspicious.

253
00:13:45.970 --> 00:13:46.900
Let's run.

254
00:13:46.900 --> 00:13:47.640
Okay.

255
00:13:47.870 --> 00:13:50.060
Untie me! Damn it!

256
00:13:52.980 --> 00:13:54.140
Bye.

257
00:13:54.140 --> 00:13:58.280
Hey, you two, get back
here or you're gonna die!

258
00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:05.160
There's just this one guy?

259
00:14:05.170 --> 00:14:08.200
Maybe he just drifted here from
real far out or something.

260
00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:09.830
Yeah, right.

261
00:14:09.840 --> 00:14:11.960
Those guys are dead
and they don't even know it.

262
00:14:11.970 --> 00:14:14.720
Or maybe somebody just wanted
him to die real slowly.

263
00:14:14.720 --> 00:14:17.500
I think we
should take him to Arlong.

264
00:14:18.290 --> 00:14:19.810
Forgive me, Zoro.

265
00:14:19.810 --> 00:14:22.840
I will tell Luffy that you were
courageous to the bitter end.

266
00:14:22.850 --> 00:14:26.700
Please forgive me, Zoro!
I'll never forget you!

267
00:14:26.700 --> 00:14:28.850
Okay, now let's find some land.

268
00:14:28.870 --> 00:14:30.020
Right.

269
00:14:33.860 --> 00:14:36.860
I think
this place is called Gosa Village.

270
00:14:51.810 --> 00:14:56.080
Uh. What happened here?

271
00:14:56.220 --> 00:15:01.510
I heard Arlong came through here a few
weeks back but I never thought that...

272
00:15:01.890 --> 00:15:04.840
Everything's upside down!

273
00:15:04.860 --> 00:15:07.850
I've heard people say that
fishmen can be stronger than

274
00:15:07.960 --> 00:15:10.930
normal human beings by
a very wide margin.

275
00:15:11.230 --> 00:15:15.520
I guess this is how strong you have
to be to survive the Grand Line.

276
00:15:20.340 --> 00:15:24.190
Maybe, but even the
street's upside down.

277
00:15:24.950 --> 00:15:28.070
The monster Momoo
caused this destruction.

278
00:15:28.110 --> 00:15:29.780
Monster?

279
00:15:30.920 --> 00:15:33.420
Don't tell me this place has monsters.

280
00:15:33.420 --> 00:15:37.040
We caught him out on the Grand Line
and brought him back here with us.

281
00:15:37.060 --> 00:15:38.980
From the Grand Line, huh...?

282
00:15:38.980 --> 00:15:41.340
Wait... We?

283
00:15:42.530 --> 00:15:45.340
You! You were with
that guy from the boat!

284
00:15:47.520 --> 00:15:48.390
Later!

285
00:15:48.390 --> 00:15:49.850
Come back here!

286
00:15:50.390 --> 00:15:55.480
That was close.
I wish you luck.

287
00:15:55.810 --> 00:15:59.770
I'll just hold my position here and wait
here for our backup from Yosaku and Luffy.

288
00:16:00.380 --> 00:16:02.570
You may be a fishman,

289
00:16:02.880 --> 00:16:05.190
but there is no way you can
catch me on dry land.

290
00:16:05.420 --> 00:16:07.280
I'm a very fast runner!

291
00:16:07.320 --> 00:16:10.030
I'm a beautiful gazelle.

292
00:16:10.120 --> 00:16:13.910
What the...?

293
00:16:14.310 --> 00:16:15.870
Got you, stupid fishman!

294
00:16:16.110 --> 00:16:18.420
And now I'll avenge my
father by killing you!

295
00:16:21.900 --> 00:16:22.790
Honestly.

296
00:16:23.420 --> 00:16:28.590
<b>Chabo
Gosa Town Nojiko
Cocoyashi Village</b>

297
00:16:24.420 --> 00:16:27.760
How many times do I have to tell you, Chabo,
you do not mess with the fishmen?

298
00:16:27.760 --> 00:16:30.010
It was just one person who
decided to stand up to them

299
00:16:30.020 --> 00:16:33.060
and they responded by
slaughtering everyone in Gosa.

300
00:16:34.530 --> 00:16:36.670
Hm. You look and
smell just like a fishman,

301
00:16:36.670 --> 00:16:39.390
but I can see that
you're human. Mostly human.

302
00:16:39.510 --> 00:16:41.210
Ah! Mostly?!

303
00:16:41.210 --> 00:16:43.440
Where'd you go? Over here?

304
00:16:43.780 --> 00:16:44.940
Crap.

305
00:16:45.040 --> 00:16:46.250
A fishman!

306
00:16:46.250 --> 00:16:47.950
And this time it's for real.

307
00:16:50.080 --> 00:16:52.410
Alright. Stand back
and let me handle this one.

308
00:16:52.720 --> 00:16:56.250
Watch as Captain Usopp... takes out
this fishman with a single shot.

309
00:16:58.000 --> 00:16:59.040
Take this.

310
00:16:59.040 --> 00:17:02.330
It's my
Special Attack: Lead Star.

311
00:17:08.700 --> 00:17:10.840
I guess he wasn't listening
when I said the fishmen

312
00:17:10.840 --> 00:17:12.340
would kill us if we messed with them.

313
00:17:12.340 --> 00:17:13.510
Come on, tough guy...

314
00:17:14.260 --> 00:17:20.770
<b>Outskirts of Cocoyashi Village</b>

315
00:17:22.500 --> 00:17:26.320
Where am I?

316
00:17:26.340 --> 00:17:27.510
My house.

317
00:17:27.510 --> 00:17:29.340
H... Huh?

318
00:17:29.340 --> 00:17:30.350
Sleep well?

319
00:17:30.350 --> 00:17:31.860
Uh. Who are you?

320
00:17:31.880 --> 00:17:35.490
I'm Nojiko. I grow
tangerines here. Want one?

321
00:17:35.490 --> 00:17:38.700
That's right! You're the
one that hit me on the head.

322
00:17:38.830 --> 00:17:42.720
Just when I was going to save you.

323
00:17:42.720 --> 00:17:44.470
I'm the one who saved you.

324
00:17:44.470 --> 00:17:45.000
Huh?

325
00:17:45.010 --> 00:17:46.880
If you had
actually gone through with

326
00:17:47.150 --> 00:17:50.550
attacking that fishman, you
would have been killed for sure.

327
00:17:50.710 --> 00:17:52.010
Stupid outsider.

328
00:17:54.340 --> 00:17:57.140
You'd figure a kid from here
would already know better.

329
00:17:58.050 --> 00:18:02.100
What would make a child
do something so reckless?

330
00:18:02.110 --> 00:18:04.860
That's a question I'd really
like an answer for.

331
00:18:05.180 --> 00:18:06.610
I know... I know!

332
00:18:07.180 --> 00:18:11.180
But they killed my daddy.
They took everything from me.

333
00:18:11.180 --> 00:18:14.110
Those fishmen destroyed
our town, killed my friends!

334
00:18:14.800 --> 00:18:17.580
I had to make them pay for
what they did, no matter what!

335
00:18:18.000 --> 00:18:19.660
Don't you get that?!

336
00:18:19.670 --> 00:18:22.830
So I went to Arlong Park by myself.

337
00:18:22.840 --> 00:18:25.540
But this girl stopped me from going in.

338
00:18:29.730 --> 00:18:32.470
She's like an evil witch!

339
00:18:32.470 --> 00:18:35.450
I can't stand this!
I have to avenge my father.

340
00:18:35.450 --> 00:18:37.010
I don't care if I die.

341
00:18:37.120 --> 00:18:38.260
Then die.

342
00:18:39.620 --> 00:18:42.430
If you're truly
prepared to die, then go.

343
00:18:42.430 --> 00:18:45.850
But you had better understand,
boy... I stopped you.

344
00:18:46.130 --> 00:18:48.940
And this witch you hate kept you
from carrying out your revenge.

345
00:18:49.370 --> 00:18:51.440
So far you've cheated death twice.

346
00:18:53.260 --> 00:18:54.700
Just finish your tea and go.

347
00:18:54.920 --> 00:18:57.610
Hey, you're being a little
rough on 'em, don't you think?

348
00:18:57.610 --> 00:18:59.640
I don't care who he is.

349
00:18:59.640 --> 00:19:02.750
If he wants to kill himself,
then so be it.

350
00:19:02.750 --> 00:19:06.080
He doesn't have what it
takes to suffer for revenge.

351
00:19:06.090 --> 00:19:07.330
What?

352
00:19:07.590 --> 00:19:08.790
It takes time.

353
00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:10.880
I suffer, as well.

354
00:19:10.890 --> 00:19:13.840
Revenge is not an easy
path for one to carve out.

355
00:19:15.060 --> 00:19:17.090
And to die just because
you're too foolish

356
00:19:17.500 --> 00:19:19.970
for patience is
nothing but a coward's plan.

357
00:19:22.730 --> 00:19:26.100
Wh... What do you want from me?

358
00:19:26.870 --> 00:19:29.310
I can't stand
the way I feel but...

359
00:19:30.050 --> 00:19:31.270
How's your mom?

360
00:19:33.220 --> 00:19:35.280
She's alive.

361
00:19:37.160 --> 00:19:40.530
Then go back home.
She's worried about you.

362
00:19:51.260 --> 00:19:53.260
For a chick with tattoos,

363
00:19:53.260 --> 00:19:54.800
you're actually really sweet.

364
00:19:54.800 --> 00:19:59.220
Piss off... It's time you told me
why you decided to come here to our village.

365
00:19:59.430 --> 00:20:01.100
Oh, right!

366
00:20:01.140 --> 00:20:03.170
My name is Captain Usopp.

367
00:20:03.170 --> 00:20:05.520
I'm looking for a girl named Nami.

368
00:20:08.140 --> 00:20:11.740
No way! She's a part
of the Arlong crew?!

369
00:20:11.740 --> 00:20:13.730
It certainly looks that way.

370
00:20:13.750 --> 00:20:16.780
Everybody here knows that cow.
Even the little boy.

371
00:20:17.120 --> 00:20:19.360
It gets better though.
That cow is my sister.

372
00:20:20.120 --> 00:20:21.070
We grew up here.

373
00:20:21.850 --> 00:20:25.410
Well, technically she's my adopted
sister, since we were both orphans.

374
00:20:27.860 --> 00:20:30.040
But a sister's a sister,
you know what I mean?

375
00:20:32.560 --> 00:20:34.550
I don't believe it.

376
00:20:35.760 --> 00:20:37.060
Nami's house?!

377
00:20:37.060 --> 00:20:40.300
It's mine too. We were
raised together in this house.

378
00:20:40.730 --> 00:20:45.060
She's the closest thing to family
I have left since our foster mother died.

379
00:20:45.380 --> 00:20:47.920
The three of us
used to be so happy together

380
00:20:47.920 --> 00:20:49.270
in Cocoyashi Village.

381
00:20:51.790 --> 00:20:53.520
So...

382
00:20:53.530 --> 00:20:56.990
You're telling me that Nami betrayed
her mother, her sister and her whole village

383
00:20:56.990 --> 00:20:59.360
just to be a part of Arlong's crew?

384
00:20:59.360 --> 00:21:02.950
Yeah, pretty much.
A real witch, huh?

385
00:21:03.830 --> 00:21:06.080
Damn. Nami is a total witch.

386
00:21:06.160 --> 00:21:08.710
She had us completely
fooled the entire time.

387
00:21:08.830 --> 00:21:11.630
To think she was just after
the treasure for herself.

388
00:21:11.780 --> 00:21:14.840
Even after she risked her
life to save my village.

389
00:21:14.950 --> 00:21:18.970
I don't understand.
She seemed so happy with us.

390
00:21:18.990 --> 00:21:21.300
Yeah? She was happy?

391
00:21:21.460 --> 00:21:23.700
Huh... My sister.

392
00:21:23.700 --> 00:21:27.930
We came here to try to convince
her to come back with us,

393
00:21:27.930 --> 00:21:30.480
but I guess now that's pointless.

394
00:21:34.360 --> 00:21:36.400
I just remembered that
a shipmate of mine

395
00:21:37.060 --> 00:21:40.930
was taken prisoner by the
fishmen before we got here.

396
00:21:40.930 --> 00:21:43.410
Oh, I'm in trouble. I hope he's okay.

397
00:21:43.970 --> 00:21:45.470
I hope he's at least not dead.

398
00:21:45.470 --> 00:21:48.080
Open the gates!

399
00:21:48.260 --> 00:21:50.540
We have a prisoner on board this vessel!

400
00:22:01.310 --> 00:22:02.840
One more time.

401
00:22:02.910 --> 00:22:05.850
What was your purpose in
coming here to this island?

402
00:22:06.910 --> 00:22:11.100
Like I said before, I'm looking
for a girl, you half-fish bastard.

403
00:22:11.680 --> 00:22:15.610
Wow!
For someone I'd consider a good meal,

404
00:22:15.840 --> 00:22:19.510
you are either really stupid or
you've got a lot of guts in there.

405
00:22:19.510 --> 00:22:23.030
We fishmen are, simply, the
next rung up the evolutionary

406
00:22:23.140 --> 00:22:25.030
ladder from you pathetic humans.

407
00:22:25.340 --> 00:22:26.990
We are incredibly resilient.

408
00:22:27.180 --> 00:22:29.740
We can breathe both on
land and underwater,

409
00:22:30.050 --> 00:22:32.250
an ability which
clearly establishes our

410
00:22:32.270 --> 00:22:34.970
physical superiority over you.

411
00:22:34.970 --> 00:22:37.790
I don't know if this will make
any sense to that puny brain

412
00:22:37.920 --> 00:22:41.670
rolling around in your head, but fishmen...
are the lords of all creatures

413
00:22:42.130 --> 00:22:44.840
and to fight against us
is to defy nature.

414
00:22:44.960 --> 00:22:48.310
I'm really sick of listening
to your big ideas, Arlong.

415
00:22:50.770 --> 00:22:52.900
Why are you always so serious, Nami?

416
00:22:52.900 --> 00:22:55.560
You know that I wasn't
talking about you.

417
00:22:55.810 --> 00:22:57.440
You are a very special human,

418
00:22:57.440 --> 00:23:00.900
our greatest navigator and a
valued member of this crew.

419
00:23:00.900 --> 00:23:02.330
You always have been.

420
00:23:02.330 --> 00:23:07.300
Say what you will, but I'm a lot smarter
than any of you, that's for sure.

421
00:23:07.300 --> 00:23:09.950
Why did he call you
his navigator, Nami?

422
00:23:10.440 --> 00:23:13.160
You can't honestly expect me
to believe you work for him.

423
00:23:13.440 --> 00:23:15.610
Hold on, is this guy
a friend of yours, Nami?

424
00:23:15.610 --> 00:23:16.910
Don't be ridiculous.

425
00:23:16.910 --> 00:23:20.090
This is just another fool who
thought I wasn't going to steal

426
00:23:20.270 --> 00:23:22.920
all of his treasure right
out from under his nose.

427
00:23:23.790 --> 00:23:29.350
To think he actually followed me here
without knowing that shows how stupid he is.

428
00:23:29.360 --> 00:23:31.890
So this is the person you really are.

429
00:23:32.030 --> 00:23:34.810
All along I thought you
couldn't stand pirates.

430
00:23:34.830 --> 00:23:37.900
You thought wrong. It was all an act.

431
00:23:38.000 --> 00:23:39.520
And you bought the whole show.

432
00:23:42.190 --> 00:23:43.530
That's...

433
00:23:51.530 --> 00:23:53.570
I'm a pirate, plain and simple.

434
00:23:53.570 --> 00:23:56.120
And a navigator... for Arlong.

435
00:23:56.120 --> 00:24:00.920
She had
you guys completely fooled!

436
00:24:01.030 --> 00:24:03.920
It's no use. She's cold-blooded.

437
00:24:04.000 --> 00:24:08.130
She betrayed her family for money,
so you really shouldn't feel too bad.

438
00:24:09.240 --> 00:24:14.020
If I were you, I would just admit defeat
and try to forget the day you met her.

439
00:24:14.180 --> 00:24:16.640
I don't need to.

440
00:24:16.680 --> 00:24:21.560
Heh. Because I never saw anything in
her to be trusted in the first place.

441
00:24:21.750 --> 00:24:25.190
If she turned out to be a serial
killer, I wouldn't be surprised.

442
00:24:25.370 --> 00:24:27.360
Fine! Then why don't you
just get the hell out of here.

443
00:24:27.370 --> 00:24:29.110
I'm tired of your face.

444
00:24:33.990 --> 00:24:34.950
Huh?

445
00:24:40.700 --> 00:24:43.840
Hey... Anybody know why that
guy just jumped in the water?

446
00:24:44.130 --> 00:24:46.670
It looks to me like he was just
trying to get away from Nami.

447
00:24:46.670 --> 00:24:47.470
I don't blame him.

448
00:24:47.470 --> 00:24:49.220
She can be really mean sometimes.

449
00:24:49.230 --> 00:24:52.330
Maybe he's trying to escape,
any of you geniuses think of that?

450
00:24:52.330 --> 00:24:54.220
With his arms
and legs tied up?

451
00:24:54.230 --> 00:24:57.730
I gotta say that looked a lot
more like a suicide attempt to me.

452
00:24:58.000 --> 00:24:58.940
Leave him.

453
00:25:02.520 --> 00:25:04.150
That idiot!

454
00:25:16.830 --> 00:25:17.530
They're back up!

455
00:25:17.530 --> 00:25:19.210
She saved him.

456
00:25:20.370 --> 00:25:24.000
What do
you think you're doing?

457
00:25:24.570 --> 00:25:28.970
No,
what do you think you're doing?

458
00:25:30.550 --> 00:25:34.220
You're really
just a nice girl

459
00:25:34.230 --> 00:25:37.850
who can't watch one guy die.
Why don't you quit pretending?

460
00:25:38.560 --> 00:25:39.640
And you
might want to jump in

461
00:25:39.650 --> 00:25:42.100
a little quicker next time.
I thought I was dead.

462
00:25:42.650 --> 00:25:44.560
You bastard!

463
00:25:46.220 --> 00:25:48.400
Try that again and
I'll make sure you die!

464
00:25:48.520 --> 00:25:50.240
Really?

465
00:25:50.260 --> 00:25:51.740
That's a lot of bandages.

466
00:25:51.860 --> 00:25:53.530
You must have been hurt pretty bad.

467
00:25:53.860 --> 00:25:55.030
Actually, I forgot my shirt.

468
00:25:55.030 --> 00:25:58.200
Grabbed these to cover up so
you wouldn't get distracted.

469
00:26:05.540 --> 00:26:08.520
Tell me... What should
we do with this guy?

470
00:26:08.520 --> 00:26:09.510
Lock him up.

471
00:26:09.530 --> 00:26:11.630
I'll take care of him
when I have the time.

472
00:26:11.660 --> 00:26:14.390
Arlong! Hey, Arlong!

473
00:26:14.530 --> 00:26:17.680
Yeah? Well, spit it out. What is it?

474
00:26:17.690 --> 00:26:20.260
Yes, sir... This guy
didn't come here alone.

475
00:26:20.260 --> 00:26:24.980
There was another long-nosed, weird-looking
guy with him but he got away.

476
00:26:25.260 --> 00:26:26.730
What the hell, Usopp?

477
00:26:26.730 --> 00:26:29.320
You left me for dead
and got spotted anyway?

478
00:26:29.540 --> 00:26:30.360
I think...

479
00:26:30.470 --> 00:26:33.490
I think he escaped into
Cocoyashi Village.

480
00:26:34.640 --> 00:26:35.740
Cocoyashi, huh?

481
00:26:36.610 --> 00:26:39.700
That's perfect. Now I
have two reasons to go.

482
00:26:45.380 --> 00:26:48.040
<b>Cocoyashi Village</b>

483
00:26:46.210 --> 00:26:48.040
Hey, Arlong's coming!

484
00:26:48.550 --> 00:26:51.050
He is? But why?

485
00:26:51.050 --> 00:26:53.590
We just paid him this
month's tribute, didn't we?

486
00:26:54.560 --> 00:26:57.640
It's probably about
my weapons cache they found.

487
00:26:57.660 --> 00:27:00.520
Everyone go home.

488
00:27:01.310 --> 00:27:02.100
Genzo...

489
00:27:02.090 --> 00:27:03.980
They're here.

490
00:27:12.600 --> 00:27:17.370
So you're the fool who thought he
could hoard weapons on my island.

491
00:27:17.370 --> 00:27:19.740
That's me. I'm a collector.

492
00:27:19.780 --> 00:27:24.120
<b>Genzo
Cocoyashi Village</b>

493
00:27:19.970 --> 00:27:24.290
Is there a new law that forbids us
from having hobbies now, as well?

494
00:27:24.310 --> 00:27:26.170
Next, you'll be telling us
that we can't read books

495
00:27:27.070 --> 00:27:29.040
or play with our children anymore.

496
00:27:29.040 --> 00:27:31.710
No, hobbies are fine.

497
00:27:32.150 --> 00:27:34.510
It would be weapons
that I have forbidden.

498
00:27:34.510 --> 00:27:37.720
They make it difficult for me
and my men to keep the peace.

499
00:27:39.050 --> 00:27:43.270
That's him?! Arlong's gigantic!
He's not even human.

500
00:27:43.650 --> 00:27:45.350
Nope... he's a fishman.

501
00:27:45.820 --> 00:27:46.560
For real?!

502
00:27:46.990 --> 00:27:49.490
I'm responsible for
twenty towns and villages,

503
00:27:49.490 --> 00:27:52.890
including this one, and as
your leader I cannot tolerate

504
00:27:52.890 --> 00:27:55.200
even a little rebelliousness.

505
00:27:55.220 --> 00:27:59.240
Wiping out Gosa was just a small
example of what can happen

506
00:27:59.260 --> 00:28:02.260
when you do not do as you are told.

507
00:28:02.260 --> 00:28:05.330
Tribute money must be
paid no matter what.

508
00:28:05.730 --> 00:28:07.770
What? Tribute money?

509
00:28:07.770 --> 00:28:09.210
It's just what it sounds like.

510
00:28:09.270 --> 00:28:11.670
Money we pay him so we can stay alive.

511
00:28:11.690 --> 00:28:13.210
Adults and children...

512
00:28:13.230 --> 00:28:17.470
If there is even a single person who
can't pay... then what happened to Gosa...

513
00:28:17.490 --> 00:28:20.800
will happen to everyone
in this village as well.

514
00:28:21.060 --> 00:28:25.390
Our town, and the people in it,
will be wiped from existence.

515
00:28:25.400 --> 00:28:29.230
H... He destroyed an entire
town because of one person?

516
00:28:29.270 --> 00:28:31.020
That's how Arlong rules.

517
00:28:31.170 --> 00:28:35.440
To them we're nothing but a sub-species,
so killing us has always been easy.

518
00:28:35.540 --> 00:28:38.320
You pathetic humans
need to stop with all this

519
00:28:38.340 --> 00:28:41.950
"thinking" you're up to.
It's your greatest weakness.

520
00:28:42.730 --> 00:28:45.800
I'm allowing you to contribute
to greatness here!

521
00:28:45.800 --> 00:28:50.210
Soon fishmen will conquer the humans,
and your tributes will be a small part

522
00:28:50.470 --> 00:28:53.420
of the beginning of the
glorious Arlong Empire!

523
00:28:55.810 --> 00:28:57.300
Arlong Empire?!

524
00:28:58.680 --> 00:29:02.510
They're planning on taking
over the entire East Blue!

525
00:29:22.940 --> 00:29:26.870
Get outta here quick.
Arlong's gonna be back soon.

